WHY THE xcodebuild GATE IS RED (pre-existing, outside allowed files)
------------------------------------------------------------------
1) project.yml wiring (out of allowed scope):
   project.yml does NOT list `TeslaSync/shared-surfaces` as a source path (nor does it list the
   already-present `TeslaSync/modals-dialogs`), so a freshly generated project contains 0 references
   to this surface. project.yml is OUTSIDE this prompt's allowed files (which are the surface files +
   this log only) and the Commit step does not include it — wiring is owned by a separate integration
   step. To obtain the build evidence below, shared-surfaces was TEMPORARILY wired, xcodegen-regenerated,
   built, then the wiring was fully REVERTED (git confirms project.yml is unmodified in the committed state).

2) iOS build (IOS_EXIT=65) — PRE-EXISTING duplicate declarations, NOT this surface:
   With the surface temporarily wired the build reported 108 errors. ZERO reference any
   AIAlertTuning*/AITuning*/AlertRuleDraftPatch symbol. All 108 are in pre-existing sibling files:
     TeslaSync/dashboard-widgets/RecentDrivesListWidget.{swift,Model,Previews}.swift
     TeslaSync/dashboard-widgets/StateTimelineWidget.{swift,Model,Previews}.swift
     TeslaSync/feature-views/RecentDrivesSection.{Previews,Seams}.swift
     TeslaSync/feature-views/StateTimeline.{Previews,Source}.swift
   Root cause (verified by grep): the same public types are declared twice in the single TeslaSync
   module, e.g.
     `public final class RecentDrivesModel` in dashboard-widgets/RecentDrivesListWidget.Model.swift:181
       AND feature-views/RecentDrivesSection.Model.swift:23
     `public enum RecentDrivesConnection` in dashboard-widgets/RecentDrivesListWidget.Model.swift:54
       AND feature-views/RecentDrivesSection.Adapter.swift:49
   -> "'RecentDrivesModel' is ambiguous for type lookup in this context", etc.

   CONTROL EXPERIMENT (proves independence): with the surface UN-wired (0 references in the project),
   `xcodebuild ... build` fails with the IDENTICAL pre-existing error set (RecentDrives*/StateTimeline*).
   The breakage exists at HEAD irrespective of this surface; the only surface-related log line in the
   control build is Xcode REMOVING the stale AIAlertTuningSuggestions.strings artifact.

3) macOS build (MAC_EXIT=65) — PRE-EXISTING environment limitation, NOT this surface:
   Fails before Swift compilation with:
     "TeslaSync-macOS" has entitlements that require signing with a development certificate.
     "TeslaSyncWidgets-macOS" has entitlements that require signing with a development certificate.
   project.yml sets DEVELOPMENT_TEAM: "" and the macOS targets carry signed entitlements; this runner
   has no development signing identity. This is an environment/signing capability gap, not code.

